@sen1761    Hence, by inference, it has been believed by some whalemen, that the Nor' West Passage, so long a problem to man, was never a problem to the whale. So that here, in the real living experience of living men, the prodigies related in old times of the inland Strello mountain in Portugal near whose top there was said to be a lake in which the wrecks of ships floated up to the surface; and that still more wonderful story of the Arethusa fountain near Syracuse whose waters were believed to have come from the Holy Land by an underground passage; these fabulous narrations are almost fully equalled by the realities of the whalemen.

