@sen2125    Then all in one welded commotion came an invisible push from astern, while forward the boat seemed striking on a ledge; the sail collapsed and exploded; a gush of scalding vapor shot up near by; something rolled and tumbled like an earthquake beneath us.

              " (extract-fr) section with name: the first lowering. [numbered in the document as: 48.]

@sen2126    The whole crew were half suffocated as they were tossed helter-skelter into the white curdling cream of the squall.

              " (extract-fr) section with name: the first lowering. [numbered in the document as: 48.]

@sen2129    Swimming round it we picked up the floating oars, and lashing them across the gunwale, tumbled back to our places.

              " (extract-fr) section with name: the first lowering. [numbered in the document as: 48.]

@sen2131   The wind increased to a howl; the waves dashed their bucklers together; the whole squall roared, forked, and crackled around us like a white fire upon the prairie, in which, unconsumed, we were burning; immortal in these jaws of death!

              " (extract-fr) section with name: the first lowering. [numbered in the document as: 48.]

@sen2132    In vain we hailed the other boats; as well roar to the live coals down the chimney of a flaming furnace as hail those boats in that storm.

              " (extract-fr) section with name: the first lowering. [numbered in the document as: 48.]

