@sen3271   One old Sag-Harbor whaleman's chief reason for questioning the Hebrew story was this:—He had one of those quaint old-fashioned Bibles, embellished with curious, unscientific plates; one of which represented Jonah's whale with two spouts in his head—a peculiarity only true with respect to a species of the Leviathan the Right Whale, and the varieties of that order, concerning which the fishermen have this saying, "A penny roll would choke him"; his swallow is so very small.

