              " (extract-fr) section with name: the fountain. [numbered in the document as: 85.]

@sen3330   Furthermore, as his windpipe solely opens into the tube of his spouting canal, and as that long canal—like the grand Erie Canal—is furnished with a sort of locks that open and shut for the downward retention of air or the upward exclusion of water, therefore the whale has no voice; unless you insult him by saying, that when he so strangely rumbles, he talks through his nose.

              " (extract-fr) section with name: the fountain. [numbered in the document as: 85.]

@sen3331    But then again, what has the whale to say?

              " (extract-fr) section with name: the fountain. [numbered in the document as: 85.]

