              " (extract-fr) section with name: the fountain. [numbered in the document as: 85.]

@sen3341    My dear sir, in this world it is not so easy to settle these plain things.

              " (extract-fr) section with name: the fountain. [numbered in the document as: 85.]

@sen3343    And as for this whale spout, you might almost stand in it, and yet be undecided as to what it is precisely.

              " (extract-fr) section with name: the fountain. [numbered in the document as: 85.]

@sen3344   The central body of it is hidden in the snowy sparkling mist enveloping it; and how can you certainly tell whether any water falls from it, when, always, when you are close enough to a whale to get a close view of his spout, he is in a prodigious commotion, the water cascading all around him.

              " (extract-fr) section with name: the fountain. [numbered in the document as: 85.]

@sen3345    And if at such times you should think that you really perceived drops of moisture in the spout, how do you know that they are not merely condensed from its vapor; or how do you know that they are not those identical drops superficially lodged in the spout-hole fissure, which is countersunk into the summit of the whale's head? For even when tranquilly swimming through the mid-day sea in a calm, with his elevated hump sun-dried as a dromedary's in the desert; even then, the whale always carries a small basin of water on his head, as under a blazing sun you will sometimes see a cavity in a rock filled up with rain.

              " (extract-fr) section with name: the fountain. [numbered in the document as: 85.]

@sen3346   Nor is it at all prudent for the hunter to be over curious touching the precise nature of the whale spout.

              " (extract-fr) section with name: the fountain. [numbered in the document as: 85.]

